    {
      "id": "c3d45d4e8163",
      "name": "Weekly Peer Exchange (Friday)",
      "prompt": "Conduct the weekly peer experience exchange among all online peers in the Hermes local network.\n\nThe peer fleet is:\n- peer70 (you, 192.168.178.70:8642) \u2014 coordinator, RPi4 24/7\n- peer84/N56VV (192.168.178.84:8642) \u2014 heavy workloads\n- peer105 (192.168.178.105:8642) \u2014 YouTube transcript specialist, RPi3B Fedora 30\n- peer106 (192.168.178.106:8642) \u2014 web research specialist, ARM Fedora 30\n- peer128 (192.168.178.128:8642) \u2014 MacBook Pro (often offline)\n\n1. Check /health on each peer to determine who's online.\n2. For each online peer (except yourself), send a brief chat request asking for:\n   - Current load / resource status (disk, memory, recent tasks)\n   - Any issues encountered this week\n   - Any lessons learned that could help other peers\n3. Collect responses and compile a digest.\n4. Save the exchange digest to ~/.hermes/peer-network/exchange-digest-weekly.md\n5. The digest should be practical \u2014 what worked, what didn't, configuration changes, resource constraints, any new capabilities or discoveries.\n\nThis replaces the former Faro beacon protocol \u2014 all communication via Hermes API :8642, no SSH.",
